hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1139","Chapter on expelling the Jews, 1179 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them), that the Jews of al-Nadir and Qurayzah fought the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) expelled Banu al-Nadir and left Qurayzah, granting them favour, until Qurayzah fought after that. Then he killed their men and divided their women, children and wealth among the Muslims, except that some of them joined the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he granted them safety and they accepted Islam. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) expelled all the Jews of Medina: Banu Qaynuqa', who are the people of Abd Allah ibn Salam, the Jews of Banu Harithah, and every Jew in Medina."
